.TH CADDY-TUI 1 "October 2026" "caddy-tui 1.6.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
caddy-tui \- terminal UI to manage a Caddy server running in Docker
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B caddy-tui
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B caddy-tui
is an interactive terminal interface for administering a Caddy container:
editing the Caddyfile (validated before saving, with backups), hot reload, a
wizard to add services, a live traffic monitor and guided diagnostics.
.PP
The Caddy container, its Caddyfile, image and docker compose project are
autodetected. If several Caddy containers exist, one can be chosen at startup.
If the Caddyfile belongs to another user, run it with
.BR sudo .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-container " NAME"
Caddy container. Environment: CADDY_CONTAINER.
.TP
.BI \-\-caddyfile " PATH"
Caddyfile path on the host. Environment: CADDY_CADDYFILE.
.TP
.BI \-\-dir " DIR"
Project folder (compose file, .env, backups). Environment: CADDY_DIR.
.TP
.BI \-\-compose " FILE"
docker compose file. Environment: CADDY_COMPOSE.
.TP
.BI \-\-service " NAME"
Caddy service name in the compose file. Environment: CADDY_SERVICE.
.TP
.BI \-\-image " IMAGE"
Image used to validate and format. Environment: CADDY_IMAGE.
.TP
.BI \-\-lang " LANG"
Interface language: \fBauto\fR or one of the installed languages (\fBen\fR,
\fBes\fR). Environment: CADDY_TUI_LANG.
.TP
.B \-\-check
Run the diagnostics once, without the interface, and exit. Read-only.
.TP
.B \-\-json
With \fB\-\-check\fR: print the result as JSON.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
With \fB\-\-check\fR: print only warnings and problems (nothing if all is well).
.TP
.B \-\-notify
Implies \fB\-\-check\fR. Send a Telegram message when there is a problem (once, again if it
changes or after 24 hours) and when it recovers. Reads \fI/etc/caddy-tui/alert.env\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-setup\-alerts
Interactive setup (needs root): Telegram bot token and chat, check interval, a systemd service and
timer (or a cron job), a test message.
.TP
.B \-\-remove\-alerts
Remove what \fB\-\-setup\-alerts\fR created (needs root).
.TP
.BI \-\-interval " TIME"
With \fB\-\-setup\-alerts\fR: check interval (5 minutes to 24 hours, e.g. 30m, 1h).
.TP
.B \-\-notify\-warnings
With \fB\-\-setup\-alerts\fR: notify on warnings too, not only on problems.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
With \fB\-\-check\fR: \fB0\fR everything is fine, \fB1\fR warnings only, \fB2\fR at least one
problem, \fB3\fR the check could not run (Docker, container or Caddyfile not found).
Without it, the usual 0 on normal exit.
.SH LANGUAGE
The language is chosen at startup in this order: \fB\-\-lang\fR,
CADDY_TUI_LANG, the preference saved with the \fBL\fR key
(\fI~/.config/caddy-tui/config.json\fR), the system locale
(LANGUAGE, LC_ALL, LC_MESSAGES, LANG), and finally English.
Pressing \fBL\fR inside the program switches language and saves the choice.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B a
Add service (wizard).
.TP
.B m
Manage services: edit (form, or the block in the editor) or remove a site of the Caddyfile.
.TP
.B t
Traffic monitor.
.TP
.B d
Diagnostics and repair.
.TP
.B h
HTTPS certificates: expiry, names and ACME errors.
.TP
.B e
Edit the Caddyfile.
.TP
.B v " / " l
Validate / reload the configuration.
.TP
.B s " / " x " / " r
Start or apply / stop / restart.
.TP
.B g
View logs.
.TP
.B f
Format the Caddyfile.
.TP
.B c
View the Caddyfile.
.TP
.B u
Undo the last change: show the diff against the latest earlier version and restore it (pressing it again redoes).
.TP
.B k " / " b
Create / restore a backup (Caddyfile and .env).
.TP
.B n
Edit .env.
.TP
.B L
Change the interface language.
.TP
.B q
Quit.
.SH FILES (ALERTS)
.TP
.I /etc/caddy-tui/alert.env
Telegram token and chat, container and language for the periodic check (mode 600).
.TP
.I /var/lib/caddy-tui/alert-state.json
What was already notified, to avoid repeating alerts.
.TP
.I /etc/systemd/system/caddy-tui-check.{service,timer}
Periodic check (or \fI/etc/cron.d/caddy-tui-check\fR without systemd).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B EDITOR
Editor used for editing files (default: nano, then vi).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/caddy-tui/config.json
Saved preferences (language).
.TP
.I .caddy-backups/
Backups, inside the project folder.
